PERIODIC TABLE DIRECTIONAL TRENDS
Fundamentals: Z_eff (effective nuclear charge) ↑ left→right
              n (principal shell) ↑ down a group
Variables:    Z (atomic number), r (atomic radius),
              χ (electronegativity), IE (ionisation energy),
              OS (oxidation state)

┌─────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┐
│ ELECTRONEGATIVITY (χ)       │ MASS & Z                    │ ELECTROPOSITIVITY           │
│                             │                             │                             │
│  F strongest                │  Z and mass generally       │  Cs/Fr lose e⁻ easiest      │
│  ↑                          │  ↑                          │  ↓                          │
│  ←─────────────→            │  ←─────────────→            │  ←─────────────→            │
│  increases L→R              │  increases L→R              │  decreases L→R              │
│  decreases down group       │  increases down group       │  increases down group       │
└─────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────┘

┌─────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┐
│ OXIDATION STATES (OS)       │ ATOMIC RADIUS (r)           │ ELEMENTAL HYDRIDES          │
│                             │                             │                             │
│  valence e⁻ config          │  ••••                       │  Ionic   Metallic  Covalent │
│  common OS shown            │  •••••                      │  (left)  (middle)  (right)  │
│  e.g. C: +4,+2,-4           │  ••••••                     │                             │
│  transition metals          │  •••••••                    │         Hydride Gap         │
│  variable OS                │  ↓ r ↑ down group           │                             │
│                             │  r ↓ L→R (Z_eff ↑)          │                             │
└─────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────┘

┌─────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┐
│ METALLIC PROPERTIES         │ ORGANIC CHEMISTRY           │ 1st IONISATION ENERGY (IE)  │
│                             │                             │                             │
│  metals (left/bottom)       │  C H O N  (most common)     │  He/F highest               │
│  nonmetals (right/top)      │  less common: S,P,halogens  │  ↑                          │
│  metalloids (diagonal)      │                             │  ←─────────────→            │
│  metallic character         │                             │  increases L→R              │
│  ↑ down group, ↓ L→R        │                             │  increases up a group       │
└─────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────┘

┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ INORGANIC CHEMISTRY                                                                     │
│ Every element is special. Covers all elements + compounds outside C-H-O-N framework.    │
│ Types: metals, nonmetals, metalloids, ionic/covalent/metallic compounds, hydrides,      │
│        oxides, coordination complexes, etc.                                             │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

Core reason behind the arrows:
Across a period  → nucleus gains protons (Z ↑) while n stays same → Z_eff ↑ → electrons held tighter
Down a group     → new electron shell added (n ↑) → size ↑, outer e⁻ farther from nucleus
